From 9bb4255504ba964da0ee6c9b5d25db5fbbb8d884 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:00:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: admit the first EAPOL-Key on the station tag
 before activation

In boots AA and AA3 the access point's first EAPOL-Key arrived 24 ms
after the status-0 association response. It carried the firmware's
BSSID tag 1, the station record the association created, before the
driver had activated that record: the post-association path waits for
the BSS record's credit and then the station record's before it sets
join_sta_active. The receive gate admitted tag 1 only while the station
was active, so the frame was refused at bss-interval. The handshake
resumed only on the access point's retransmission 996 ms later, on half
of the retained connects.

Tag 1 is now admitted from the accepted association on, with every
other condition unchanged: a status-0 association response received,
the deauthentication not done, no cleanup, and at most two delivered
EAPOL-Key frames per lifetime. Tag 15 keeps its interval (only until
the BSS command's credit), and any other tag is still refused. Only the
timing relaxes. The supplicant's reply was already held in the transmit
queue until the station activation, and it still is.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c | 18 ++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
index e85f9b484..bbe6a4750 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
@@ -5013,18 +5013,20 @@ static void mt6797_mac_join_work(struct work_struct *work)
 			    mac->join_eapol_seen < 2 &&
 			    /* BSSID tag 15, observed before the station activation
 			     * (runtimes 12 and 15, message 1), is admitted only until the
-			     * successful BSS command credit completion is recorded; tag 1,
-			     * observed after the station activation (runtime 15, the next
-			     * EAPOL-shaped packet after the activation event, refused at
-			     * this field; expected to be message 3, unvalidated), only
-			     * while the station is active. The field is filled by the
-			     * firmware and unused by the pinned receive path; each value is
-			     * bound to the interval in which it was measured, and any other
+			     * successful BSS command credit completion is recorded; tag 1
+			     * from the accepted association on. Tag 1 was first observed
+			     * after the station activation (runtime 15, message 3), and
+			     * boots AA and AA3 observed it on message 1, 24 ms after the
+			     * association response and before the activation, where waiting
+			     * for the activation cost the access point's one-second
+			     * retransmission (0305). The supplicant's reply still waits for
+			     * the activation in the transmit queue. The field is filled by
+			     * the firmware and unused by the pinned receive path; any other
 			     * value is refused and named by the frame gate below. The rest
 			     * of the decoder's framing gates verify that packet next.
 			     */
 			    ((eapol.bss_index == 15 && !mac->join_bss_configured) ||
-			     (eapol.bss_index == 1 && mac->join_sta_active))) {
+			     eapol.bss_index == 1)) {
 				mt6797_mac_eapol_trace(mac, rx.logical_bytes, "admitted", "ok",
 						       eapol_gate, eapol.bytes);
 				mac->join_eapol_seen++;
